      "message": "Agreed!. Here\u0027s what I parsed.\n\n   \n    // kind of assertion\n    if library \u003d\u003d nil {\n        return false\n    }\n\n    // vndk-ext is public to use-vndk libs\n    if c.IsVndkExt() {\n        return false\n    }\n\n    // llndk-public(?) is public to use-vndk libs\n    if Bool(library.Properties.Llndk.Vendor_available) {\n        return false\n    }\n\n    // old legacy from when VNDK-private is vendor_available: false?\n    // can we remove this condition?\n    if c.VendorProperties.Vendor_available !\u003d nil \u0026\u0026 !Bool(c.VendorProperties.Vendor_available) {\n        return true\n    }\n\n    // vndk \u0026\u0026 private\n    if c.vndkdep !\u003d nil \u0026\u0026 Bool(c.vndkdep.Properties.Vndk.Private) {\n        return true\n    }\n\n    return false\n\n\nI think this func should be something like\n\n    // vndk \u0026\u0026 private\n    return c.vndkdep !\u003d nil \u0026\u0026 Bool(c.vndkdep.Properties.Vndk.Private)",
